1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Disputed as wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Atanagildo-II-rey-de-los-visigodos/6000000003040988215?through=6000000003975586314 or mother of https://www.geni.com/people/Ardevaste-the-Greek-Balthes-Prince-of-the-
2 CONC Visigoths/6000000189160702845#/tab/discussion
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT Her ancestry is speculative. According to Salazar y Castro she was a relative of the Emperor Mauricius.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some sources show her as a daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Petrus-Augustus/6000000013790902482 (c.550-602), curopalates and brother of the Emperor Mauricius, and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Anastasia-Aerobinda/600
2 CONC 0000001412968342 (born c.570), in turn a daughter of Areobindus (born c.550) and his wife, a paternal granddaughter of a certain Anastasius (c.530-after 571) and Juliana (born c.533, married after 548) and a great-granddaughter of
2 CONC  Flavius Anastasius Paulus Probus Sabinianus Pompeius (c.500-after 517), Roman consul in 517. This Pompeius' wife was Theodora (born c.515), natural daughter of the Empress Theodora.
2 CONT
2 CONT Doria suggests she might have been a daughter of Vardanes Mamikonian, a possible nephew of Artavazd IV, married about 578 in Byzantium to a daughter of Philippicos and Gordia (who was sister of Mauricius).
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT According to http://bloodroyal.tripod.com/CleopatraVII.html this person (the daughter of Georgia and mother of Ardebasto) is Juliana, wife of Atanagildo, Visi-Goth Prince of Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingund_(wife_of_Hermenegild)
2 CONT
2 CONT 17th-century Spanish genealogist Luis Bartolomé de Salazar y Castro gave Ardabast's father as Athanagild, the son of Saint Hermenegild and Ingund, and his mother as Flavia Juliana, a daughter of Peter Augustus and niece of the Emp
2 CONC eror Maurice.[20] This imperial connection is disputed by Christian Settipani, who says that the only source for Athanagild's marriage to Flavia Julia is José Pellicer, who he claims to be a forger.[21]
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT sobrinha do Imperador Maurício, do Império Romano do Oriente
