2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Descendants===
2 CONT
2 CONT He married the natural daughter of Empress Theodora, born about 515, although Emperor Justinian I apparently treated her and her son Athanasius as fully legitimate, and had:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Anastasius
2 CONT # John
2 CONT # Athanasius
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Identity
2 CONT
2 CONT Cameron in his “Stemma” shows the three sons of the daughter of Theodora as the grandsons of Caesaria, sister of Emperor Anastasius, and Caesaria's husband Secundinus, who was consul in 511. Cameron shows Theodora's son in law as 
2 CONC an unnamed son either of Caesaria's son Probus (consul in 502 and alive in 542) or Caesaria's daughter Caesaria, who died in 556.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Sabinianus-1
2 CONT
2 CONT Cameron shows Flavius Anastasius Paulus Probus Sabinianus Pompeius Anastatasius, consul in 517, as the son of Sabinianus, consul in 505, and his unnamed wife, a niece of emperor Anastasius I
2 CONT
2 CONT This Anastasius is often thought to be the father of Anastasius, who married the unnamed daughter of Theodora.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cameron [2] distinguishes them, nothing that Anastasius son of Sabinianus is a nephew of Emperor Anastasius I in the male line, and Anastasius, grandson of Theodora, would be addressed in his male line relationship if it existed r
2 CONC ather than simply as the grandson of Theodora.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Anastasius and John, and St. Athanasius [3]
2 CONT
