1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Théodora, later the Empress Théodora, has a daughter born by the year 515.  We don’t know the name of the daughter or the name of her father.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodora_(6th_century)_
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of 16, Theodora traveled to North Africa as the companion of a Syrian official named Hecebolus when he went to the Libyan Pentapolis as governor.[11] She stayed with him for almost four years before returning to Constan
2 CONC tinople. Abandoned and maltreated by Hecebolus, on her way back to the capital of the Byzantine Empire, she settled for a while in Alexandria, Egypt. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Orientalism and the Reception of Powerful Women from the Ancient World edited by Filippo Carlà-Uhink, Anja Wieber [https://books.google.com/books?id=2wvBDwAAQBAJ&lpg=PA313&ots=GVJNysdtbV&dq=Hecebolus%20%22The%20Tyrian%22&pg=PA31
