1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paulus_(consul_496)_
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Paulus (floruit 496) was a politician of the Eastern Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Paulus was the brother of Anastasius I. His family was Illyrian,[1] and he was the son of Pompeius (born c. 410), a nobleman from Dyrrachium, and Anastasia Constantina (born c. 410), an Arian and a paternal great-granddaughter of 
2 CONC the Roman caesar Constantius Gallus and his wife, Constantina (the daughter of Roman emperor Constantine the Great).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT In 496 he was appointed consul without colleague. He married Magna; they had a daughter, Irene, who married Olybrius, a member of the House of Theodosius.
2 CONT
