1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was a Roman noble, and a member of the powerful gens Anicia, but his parentage is uncertain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT One theory is that he was related to the Consul Anicius Hermogenianus Olybrius, whose wife and cousin, Anicia Juliana, had the same name Olybrius gave to his own daughter. However, Juliana was a common name name among the Anicii, 
2 CONC and Hermogenianus seems to have had only one daughter, who took chastity vows. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other theories make him a son of Flavius Anicius Probus or, less probably, Petronius Maximus.
2 CONT
