2 CONT
2 CONT Licinia was at one time had children with at least three men - Flavius Valentinian of Rome III, Gensreic (Spear King) Vandals, and Petronius Maximus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Licinius Eudoxia was the daughter of the powerful Eastern Emperor Theodosius II, married off to the Western Emperors Valentinian III and his successor Petronius Maximus.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Her ancestry is found elasewhere on the tree - Licinia's father was Theodosus II and her mother was Athenais Eudocia.  Her paternal grandparents were Archadius and Aelia Eudoxia; her maternal grandparents were Leontius and <Unknow
2 CONC n>. She had three sisters named Flaccilla, Marina and Arcadia.
