1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Roman Princess; Empress of Constance III
2 CONT She was granted her own household, which made her financially independent.5
2 CONT She was summoned to Milan, and there she witnessed the death of her father in
2 CONT 395.5 She was named Most Noble Girl (Nobilissima Puella) circa 400. She seems
2 CONT to have been raised in the care of her cousin Serena, the wife of the western
2 CONT general Stilicho, and presumably received a classical education, and also knew
2 CONT how to weave and embroider.5 She was carried off with the Visigoths who sacked
2 CONT Rome to Gaul.5 She married King of the Visigoths Athaulf Balthi, son of
2 CONT Modares Balthi, in 414 in Narbonne, Gaul; His 2nd. Her 1st.2,1,3,6 She was
2 CONT finally restored to the Romans following the death of her Visigoth husband
2 CONT Athaulf in 416.5 She married Constantius III, imperator in 417 in Rome, Italy;
2 CONT Her 2nd.2,3,4,7 She and Constantius III, imperator became involved -- on the
2 CONT losing side -- in the controversy over the election of a new bishop of Rome in
2 CONT 419. She was made Augusta (Empress) in 421.
1 NOTE Galla Placidia, half-sister of Roman Emperor Honorius (b. 384- d. 423), was the daughter of Roman Emperor Theodosius ( 346-395).(father of Honorius) and his 2nd wife Galla.
2 CONT Galla Placidia, as it has been stated,  was half-sister of Honorius, who married her off, first to Ataulf of the Visigoths (414) , then to Honorius favorite General, Constantius in 417.
2 CONT
2 CONT Six years after she retired as Regent and Empress of the Western Roman Empire, acting for her son Valentianian III, Empress Galla Placidia, daughter of Emperor Theodosius and Galla, died in 450AD.  She was age 66.  She had been a 
2 CONC widow for more than twenty-nine years, and Empress-Regent for more than 19 of those years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly after the marriage of Ataulf of the Visigoths to Galla Placidia, half sister of the Roman Emperor Honorius, he died in 415 AD while invading Spain, and trying to take Barcelona.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly after he had been named AUGUSTUS of ROME, General Constantius died, leaving his wife Galla Placidia a widow for the 2nd time in 6 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alaric I of the Visigoths captured Galla Placidia, daughter of Emperor Theodosius, in 410.  She was held captive, and as a hostage until 414, when she was released and returned to her half-brother Honorius.  She then married Alari
2 CONC c's successor, Ataulf, new king of the Visigoths.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Honorius, Roman Emperor in 423, the son of Galla Placidia and General Constantius, named Valentinian III, succeeded as Roman Emperor following the short reign of Johannes from 423-425. During his minority, his m
2 CONC other Galla Placidia acted as Regent between 425 until about 444.
2 CONT
2 CONT Galla Placidia had married the Roman General Constantius, shortly the death of her 1st husband Ataulf of the Visigoths (d. 415 invading Barcelona) in 417.   She became the mother of Valentinian  in 419 who became Valentinaian III 
2 CONC  the Roman Emperor from 425-455AD.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her relase as hostage of  Alaric of the Visigoths from 41-414, Galla Placidia was returned to the care of her half-brother Honorius, who then promptly married her off.
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT http://www.art-science.com/Ken/Genealogy/PD/ch43_Early_Goths.html
2 CONT http://www.claude.barret.net/html/dat0.htm#2
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE This person, the grandaughter of Valentian I, genealogy was a tough research project to unravel.
2 CONT 1: She became a captive of the Visigoths under Alaric I who invaded Rome in 410.
2 CONT 2: The historian Jordans gives the date of 411 she married Athaulf in the Forum Livii (Forli)
2 CONT 3: Another source gave the date of marriage of Galla and Athaulf at Narbo in January of 414.
2 CONT 5: After Athaulf  dies in 415, she was traded by the King of the Visigoths, Wallia back to the Romans in return for a treaty and supplies in 416.
2 CONT 6: To her disgust she is forced to marry the Roman, Constantius.
2 CONT 7: The historical records didn't separate Galla I and Galla II and one can make the mistake of thinking that the two are one and the same when they aren't To confuse things a little more Aelia Galla Placida was the half sister of 
2 CONC Honorius and Arcadius by way of her father, Theodosius I's first marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Vito Antonio Sirago: Galla Placidia:
2 CONT e la trasformazione politca dell' occidente Louvain, 1961, Pp XXV + 556.
2 CONT (Universite' de Louvain, Recueil de Travaux d' Histoire et philogie, 4e Serie, Frasc 25.)
