2 CONC -in-law Anthemius, the choice was quite different. Aspar, who in this occasion was probably offered the throne by the Senate but refused,[3] could have chosen his own son Ardabur, but instead selected an obscure tribune of one of 
2 CONC his military units, Leo I.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 470, in an episode of the struggle for power between Aspar and the Isaurian general Zeno, Aspar persuaded the emperor to appoint his second son, Julius Patricius, as caesar and give him in marriage his daughter Leontia. However
