1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Roman Emperor ruled conjointly with his father from 383 to 395. He became the
2 CONT first
2 CONT Emperor of the East in the newly divided Empire (his brother, Honorius, became
2 CONT Emperor of the West) in 395. Emperor in Eastern Roman Empire, between 395 and
2 CONT 408.6 He was frail and ineffectual and dominated by his ministers, Rufinus,
2 CONT Eutropius, and Anthemius.2 He and Western Emperor Flavius Honorius Theodosius
2 CONT Augustus were Consul with his brother in 396. He associated his son,
2 CONT Theodosius II, with his own rule in 402.
1 NOTE Emperor of Eastern Rome from 395 until 408. Was under the control of the Vandal, Flavius Stilicho.
2 CONT Flavius Aracadius renamed the town of Selymbria (Silivri) to Eudoxiopolis after his wife died. The name never survived.
1 NOTE 1  NAME Arcadius Emperor of /Constantinople/ 1  BIRT 2  DATE APR 401
