1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Flavius Ardabur of the Alans
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife/Partner:         (missing) 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Child:         Flavius Ardabur Aspar 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lásd / See:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~jamesdow/s060/f728186.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Ardabur
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Ardaburius)
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Ardabur or Ardaburius (Greek: Φλάβιος Αρδαβούριος) served as magister militum in the Byzantine army in the 420s, under Theodosius II.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Roman-Persian War of 421, he invaded Arzanene and Mesopotamia, besieging Nisibis but at last he was defeated by Sassanid king Bahramgur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three years later, Ardabur and his son Aspar were sent on a campaign to Italy to overthrow the usurper Joannes. Ardabur was captured and held at Ravenna, where he succeeded in subverting some of the usurper's officers. Aspar was t
2 CONC hen able to capture the city and defeat Joannes.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his return to Constantinople, he was made consul for the year 427.
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Ardabur should be distinguished from his grandson of the same name, who was consul twenty years later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ardaburius
