2 CONC DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001
2 CONT
2 CONT     [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Sources: Ancestral Roots 45; Kraentzler 1669, 1680, 1795.   K-1795: Constantius I,  Emperor of Britain, Gaul, Spain and Rome ("Chlorus"). His British name appears to have been Cystennan.   K-1669: Flavius Constantius "Chlore,"
2 CONC  Emperor of Britain, Rome and Gaul.
2 CONT        Roots: Theodora Comnena, married Constantinus Angelus.
2 CONT
2 CONT     =========================
2 CONT
2 CONT          Constantinos was the governor of Dalmatia, and appointed Caesar to
2 CONT     rule Gaul and Britain March 1, 293. Born in Illyria 214, he was trained in the hard school of warfare on the Danube frontier. Constantius I became Emperor of Rome in May 305, and in right of his wife, King of England. He was b
2 CONC orn in 242 and died at Eboracum (present day York, England) on July 25, 306. The son of Helen and Constantius I was Constantine the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT     =================
