1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Lucius Plautius Lamia Silvanus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucius Plautius Lamia Silvanus (c, 110-aft. 145) was a Suffect Consul in 145.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Lucius Fundanius Laemia Aelianus and wife Annia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Aurelia Fadilla (b. ca 120), daughter of Antoninus Pius and Annia Galeria Faustina or Faustina the Elder, and had a daughter Silvana (b. ca 120), who married Marcus Annius Severus, a Suffect Consul, and they would be th
2 CONC e parents of Fabia Orestilla (ca 160 – bef. 238), wife of Gordian I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustan History claims that Fabia Orestilla was a descendant of Roman Emperors Antoninus Pius and Marcus Aurelius through her father Fulvus Antoninus. Modern historians have dismissed this name and her information as false, as th
2 CONC ey believe his wife was the granddaughter of Greek Sophist, consul and tutor Herodes Atticus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Plautius_Lamia_Silvanus
