1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Servius Cornelius Scipio Salvidienus Orfitus was a Roman senator and a consul of Rome in the year 51.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was named consul ordinarius in the year 51 as a colleague of the emperor Claudius I.[2] From 62-63, he was named proconsul of the Province of Africa by order of the emperor Nero.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his mandate in Africa finished, he fell into disgrace around the year 66 and was accused of being a traitor to the emperor Nero in the senate by Marcus Aquilius Regulus. He was found guilty and executed.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Servius_Cornelius_Scipio_Salvidienus_Orfitus_(consul_51)
