1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 522
1 DEAT
2 DATE 561
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Tegau Eurfron (of the Golden Breast)''' was one of the Three Chaste Wives of Britain. She lost her breast in battle and replaced it with one made of gold. In one version of the story, Tegau's husband Caradoc was
2 CONC  the son of a magician, Llyr Merini. During a fight over Caradoc's parentage, Llyr conjured a serpent. The serpent bit Caradoc's arm and Tegau's breast. To free herself, Tegau cut off that breast.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her virtue was celebrated in the ''Mabinogion'' (''circa'' 1060-1200), Bishop Thomas Percy's ''[http://www.lib.rochester.edu/camelot/percyboy.htm Ballad of the Boy and the Mantle] (1765)'', and Thomas Love Peacock's ''[http://www.
2 CONC thomaslovepeacock.net/Elphin.html The Misfortunes of Elphin]'' (1829).
2 CONT
2 CONT In ''Ballad of Boy and the Mantle'' Tegau owned a mantle that became one of the 13 Treasures of Britain. The mantle would reach the ground only when worn by a chaste woman, and became shorter the more faithless its wearer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Ancestry ==
2 CONT
2 CONT There are different accounts of her ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT # According to scholars, the historical Tegau was a daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Nudd-ap-Senyllt/6000000011174016373 Nudd Hael]. See David Nash Ford, [http://www.britannia.com/history/ebk/gene/strathcde.pdf Kings of Str
2 CONC athclyde, Galloway & Ynys Manaw] at [http://www.britannia.com/history/ebk/gene/ Britannica.com].
2 CONT
2 CONT # Some genealogies identify Tegau with [http://www.geni.com/people/Gwegnier-ferch-Gereint/6000000006290731029 Gwegnier ferch Gereint], daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Geraint-ab-Erbin/6000000006290680582 Gereint Llyngesog,
2 CONC  King of Dumnonia] and his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Gwyar-Amlawdd/6000000002188329233 Gwyar], a sister of King Arthur's mother. The source of the identification is not clear.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Arthurian legend calls her a daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Pellinore/6000000000437376988 King Pellinore].
