2 CONT
2 CONT '''Domitia Paulina''' or '''Paullina''', '''Domitia Paulina Major''' or '''Paulina Major''', (Major Latin for the elder), also known as '''Paulina the Elder''' (?-85/86). Paulina was a Spanish Roman woman who lived in the 1st cent
2 CONC ury. She was a daughter of a distinguished Spanish Roman senatorial family. Paulina originally came from Gades (modern Cádiz, Spain). Gades was one of the wealthiest Roman cities. Little is known of the life of Paulina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Paulina married Spanish Roman Publius Aelius Hadrianus Afer, a praetor who was a paternal cousin of Roman Emperor Trajan. Paulina and Afer had two children, a daughter Aelia Domitia Paulina (75-130) and a son emperor Publius Aeliu
2 CONC s Hadrianus (76-138). Around 85/86 Paulina died of unknown causes, before her husband. After the death of her husband, her children were raised by Trajan and the Roman officer Publius Acilius Attianus.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Augustan History - Hadrian
2 CONT * Hadrian (A.D. 117-138)
