2 CONT Tiberius Claudius Pompeianus Quintianus (170-between 212 and 217) was the son of Syrian Roman Consul Tiberius Claudius Pompeianus and Annia Aurelia Galeria Lucilla. His maternal grandparents were Roman Emperor Marcus Aurelius and 
2 CONC Roman Empress Faustina the Younger, and his uncle was Roman Emperor Commodus.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the reign of Roman Emperor Caracalla (211-217), Pompeianus was put in charge of the Roman military campaigns and awarded two consulships, one as a Suffectus in 212. However, for some reason that does not appear in the Fasti
2 CONC , he appears to have been murdered during a robbery.
