2 CONT '''[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titus_Flavius_Sabinus_(consul_69&#41 Titus Flavius Sabinus]''' was the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Titus-Flavius-Sabinus/6000000013204919137 Titus Flavius Sabinus] (consul 47). He was suffec
2 CONC t consul in May and June 69 and one of the generals who fought for Otho against Vitellius during the Year of the Four Emperors, although he submitted to Vitellius once Otho had been defeated. He was besieged alongside his father i
2 CONC n the Capital, but escaped when it was burnt down. His paternal cousin, Emperor [http://www.geni.com/people/Domitian-Roman-Emperor/6000000008059993700 Domitian], later had him put to death after a herald saluted him as imperator (
2 CONC "commander", a title only the emperor was entitled to) instead of "consul".
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of [http://www.geni.com/people/Titus-Flavius-Sabinus/6000000005379570295 Titus Flavius Sabinus] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Titus-Flavius-Clemens/6000000009144745200 Titus Flavius Clemens].
