2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Drusus Caesar=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Drusus Caesar (Latin: Drusus Julius Caesar Germanicus, 7-33) was a member of the Julio-Claudian or Imperial family of Ancient Rome. He was a son of Germanicus and Agrippina the Elder. He was brother to Emperor Caligula, nephew to 
2 CONC Emperor Claudius.
2 CONT
2 CONT Drusus married Aemilia Lepida, daughter of Marcus Aemilius Lepidus, his second cousin. Tacitus reports that during their marriage "she had pursued her husband with ceaseless accusations". In 36, she was charged with adultery with 
2 CONC a slave and committed suicide, "since there was no question about her guilt" (Tacitus, Annals 6.40).
2 CONT
2 CONT Drusus' paternal grandparents were Nero Claudius Drusus and Antonia Minor. His maternal grandparents were Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa and Julia the Elder. He was adopted by his paternal great-uncle Tiberius after Tiberius' own son, J
2 CONC ulius Caesar Drusus, had died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Drusus Caesar was later accused of plotting against Tiberius. He was exiled and imprisoned in 30, a year after his mother Agrippina the Elder and his brother Nero Caesar were arrested. He starved to death in prison in 33, reduced 
2 CONC to chewing the stuffing of his bed (Annals 6.23).
2 CONT
2 CONT His siblings included two brothers (Gaius Julius Caesar (Caligula) and Nero) and three sisters (Julia Livilla, Julia Drusilla, and Agrippina the Younger).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
