2 CONT =Gnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus, a politician of ancient Rome in the 1st century BC, was the son of Gnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus, and brother of Lucius Domitius Ahenobarbus. He married Cornelia, daughter of Lucius Cornelius Cinna, who 
2 CONC was consul in 87 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the civil war between Marius and Sulla, Ahenobarbus took the side of the former. When Sulla obtained the supreme power in 82 BC, Ahenobarbus was proscribed, and fled to Africa, where he was joined by many who were in the same c
2 CONC ondition as himself. With the assistance of the Numidian king, Hiarbas, he collected an army, but was defeated near Utica by Pompey, whom Sulla had sent against him, and was afterwards killed in the storming of his camp, in 81 BC.
2 CONC  According to some accounts, he was executed after the battle on the orders of Pompey.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gnaeus_Domitius_Ahenobarbus_(died_81_BC)
