2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavius_Probus
2 CONT =Flavius Probus, Senator=
2 CONT Flavius Probus (born ca 420, 430 or 435), a Roman Senator and a v. nob. (vir nobilis) of Narbonne, then Narbo, was a man of literary taste and precocious ability. His father was Flavius Magnus, Consul of Rome in 460. He was a frie
2 CONC nd of Sidonius Apollinaris from their schooldays.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married before 450 Eulalia (?), born ca 425, a cousin of Sidonius Apollinaris, daughter of Thaumastus. They were perhaps the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Industria of Narbonne, then Narbo, born ca 450 or 465, married before 475 to Tonantius Ferreolus
2 CONT # Firminus (455 or 460 – ca 503), v. inl. at Arles, then Arelate, and a propinq. of Magnus Felix Ennodius
2 CONT # Probatius (certain son), Bishop of Uzès in 506
