1 NOTE
2 CONT Agripinilla, also known as Agrippina the Younger, an exceeding evilwoman, sister of Caligula, fourth wife of Claudius, and the mother of L.Domitius Ahenobarbus Nero (the famous emperor).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Agrippina the Younger, born 15 A.D. and died 59 A.D., married (1) Cn.Domitus Ahenobarbus, son of Antonia the Elder, daughter of Mark Antony,and her husband, L. Domitius Ahenobarbus, who died in 40 A.D. She married(3) Claudius. The
2 CONC  child from the first marriage was L. DomitiusAhenobarbus (afterwards Nero Claudius Caesar), born in 37 A.D. and diedin 68 A.D., infamous Roman Emperor (54 AD-68 AD), who succeeded Claudius,who had ruled from 41 AD to 54 AD. This 
2 CONC Emperor Nero supposedly "fiddled"while Rome burned to the ground. He married (1) Octavia, daughter ofClaudius, and (2) Poppaea Sabina, who died in 65 A.D.
