2 CONT =Lucius Vipstanus Poplicola=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucius Vipstanus Poplicola Messalla (c. 10 – aft. 59) was a Roman politician who was Roman consul in AD 48.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT It is assumed that Vipstanus Poplicola was the son of Lucius Vipstanus Gallus and a Valeria Messalla. He was elected consul ordinarius in AD 48, alongside Aulus Vitellius. He was replaced as consul by the consul suffectus Gaius Vi
2 CONC pstanus Messalla Gallus, who is postulated to have been his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 58 or 59, Vipstanus Poplicola was appointed Proconsular governor of Asia.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the historian Ronald Syme, Vipstanus Poplicola's son was Gaius Valerius Poplicola, who was coopted into a sacerdotal college in AD 63, but died sometime after.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
