2 CONT =Lucius Antonius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Lucius Antonius (20 BC-25CE) was the eldest son of Iullus Antonius and Claudia Marcella Major. He was the grandson of triumvir Mark Antony and Octavia (sister of Augustus). No other siblings are known, but some epigraphic evidence
2 CONC  suggests he had either a sister or a daughter Iulla Antonia. His maternal half-sister was Vipsania Marcella.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was charged with adultery in 2 BCE with Julia (daughter of Augustus) and was forced to commit suicide. Lucius was sent to Marseille as a result of his father's indiscretion. In Marseille he studied law. Tacitus records 
2 CONC his death in CE 25 at Ann.4.44.4-5.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Antonius_(grandson_of_Mark_Antony)
