2 CONT =Iulla Antonia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Iulla Antonia or Julia Antonia, is thought to be a daughter of Roman consul of 10 BC Iullus Antonius and Claudia Marcella Major. Her brother was Lucius Antonius. Her maternal half-siblings were Vipsania Marcella and Appuleia Varil
2 CONC la. The only evidence of her existence is a funerary urn. It is possible she was the sister or the daughter of Lucius Antonius (or neither).
2 CONT
2 CONT Iulla’s maternal grandparents were Octavia Minor (second elder sister,and full sister to Roman Emperor Caesar Augustus) and her first husband, the Roman consul Gaius Claudius Marcellus Minor. Her paternal grandparents were Fulvia 
2 CONC and the Roman Triumvir Mark Antony. Through her paternal grandmother, she was a descendant of the Roman politician Gaius Gracchus and the Roman General Scipio Africanus Major who defeated Hannibal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Iulla was born in Rome, after 19 BC and was raised there. In 2 BC, her father was executed by her great-uncle, because he had an affair with Augustus’ daughter Julia the Elder.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iulla_Antonia
