2 CONT =Family Background & Early Life=
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturninus was of Allobrogian and Roman ancestry. He was the son of the Decimus Valerius Asiaticus[2] from his wife Vitellia,[4] the daughter of the Roman emperor Vitellius from his wife Galeria Fundana.[4] His father served as a 
2 CONC Legatus of Gallia Belgica,[2] he later became the Roman governor of that province[4] in the reign of the Roman emperor Nero.[5] The father of Saturninus, became powerful through wealth and the skilful exploitation of imperial patr
2 CONC onage.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of his father were originally from Vienna,[4] Gallia Narbonensis. Saturninus was a direct descendant of the consul, Roman Senator Decimus Valerius Asiaticus[3] and his wife Lollia Saturnina,[6] whose younger sister Loll
2 CONC ia Paulina was a Roman empress and the third wife of the Roman emperor Caligula.[7] Saturninus was a grandson[2][8] to Decimus Valerius Asiaticus and Lollia Saturnina. The name of Saturninus reveals paternally he is related to the
2 CONC  gens, Valeria, Lollia and gens, Volusia.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Vespasian became Roman emperor in second half of 69, Asiaticus was appointment for a consulship in 70.[4] Before he could serve his consulship in early 70, Asiaticus died.[9] Asiaticus was survived by Vitellia and their son.[
2 CONC 2] Later in 70, Vespasian arranged Vitellia to remarry another unnamed groom.[9] Her second marriage was a splendid match for her and Vespasian provided for her, the dowry and clothing.[9] Although he was born in Vienna, he was ra
2 CONC ised in Rome. Little is known on early life.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Political career=
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturninus started his political career in the reign of the Roman emperor Domitian who ruled from 81 til 96. He served as a Triumvir Monetalis; was a board member of the Salius collinus and the Pontiff.[10] Between the years about
2 CONC  85 to 90 he served as a Quaestor and Praetor.[11][10] Saturninus served as a suffect consul in 93[12][13] or in 94.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturninus served as a Proconsul of Asia in 108 to 109.[10] From the years 124 til 134, he served as a Praefectus urbi in Rome.[3][10] In 125, he served again as a consul.[3] During his political career in the first half of the se
2 CONC cond century, he was friends with the Roman emperors Trajan and Hadrian.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Marriage and issue=
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturninus married as his wife, the noblewoman Valeria Catulla Messallina[14][10] who came from a family of consular rank.[14] Messallina bore Asiaticus a son called Decimus Valerius Taurus Catullus Messallinus Asiaticus.[14][10]
