2 CONT
2 CONT Gaius Rubellius Blandus (?died 38) was a suffect consul of ancient Rome, a grandson of Rubellius Blandus of Tibur (see Tivoli, Italy). Blandus' family were from the Equestrian class.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Career'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Blandus was a moneyer in 4 BC; Quaestor in 1; Tribune in 6; Praetor in 11; Consul Suffectus in 18 and African Proconsul in 36.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 20 he was involved with the prosecution of Aemilia Lepida. He put forward a motion in the senate to outlaw her which was carried.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriages and Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 33 he married Julia, daughter of Livilla and consul Julius Caesar Drusus (Tacitus, Ann. 6. 27. 1). Julia was the granddaughter of Emperor Tiberius. The marriage produced two children; a boy, Rubellius Plautus who was considered
2 CONC  as a rival to Emperor Nero and Rubellia Bassa. Two further children are uncertain; a single inscription refers to a Rubellius Drusus, while Juvenal (Satire VIII. 39) suggests another son, also named Gaius Rubellius Blandus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaius_Rubellius_Blandus
