1 NOTE What's in a Name?
2 CONT
2 CONT The name "Balbi" was referenced in Phoenicia approximately 2,000 B.C. Itis thought to have derived from the word "Baal" one of two chiefdivinities at that time. The Balbi name was associated with one of themajor Phoencian cities, 
2 CONC Tyre, located on the Mediterranean Coast, and wasfamous for a rare purple dye. Now this city is named "Sur" and is locatedin what is today southern Lebanon. The Phoenicians founded the city ofGadir or Gades, now Cadiz, Spain in 11
2 CONC 00 B. C. In historical descriptionsof Gades an individual named Balbus (Latin for Balbi) was cited as thenephew of the owner Balbus. Many centuries later Julius Caesar met LuciusBalbus in Gades and subsequently brought Balbus to R
2 CONC ome. Gade'scityemblem is comprised of a single fish situated horizontally facingleft. The crest of the Balbi family of Genoa is comprised of three fishsituated horizontally facing left.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are number of famous Balbus military and political individualscited during the days of the Roman Empire, dating back to 168 B.C. Thereare also ancient Balbus sites in Rome: Balbus Theater (also shown asBalbi Theater) constru
2 CONC cted by Cornelius Balbus in 13 B. C., and CryptaBalbi.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.balbifamily.com/balbi%20news%20bytes.htm
