2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Claudia Augusta=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Claudia Augusta (Classical Latin: [ˈklawdɪa]; January 63-April 63) was the only daughter of the Roman Emperor Nero by his second wife Roman Empress Poppaea Sabina. She was born in Antium (Anzio) on 21 January 63.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nero honored Claudia and her mother with the title of Augusta. Gold statues were placed in temples and circus games were held in Claudia's honor. She died three months after her birth of illness. Nero and Poppaea Sabina mourned he
2 CONC r death and Claudia was declared a goddess. A shrine and a priest were dedicated to her shortly afterward.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claudia_Augusta
