1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulvia '''Fulvia Flacca Bambula'''] (c. 83 BC – 40 BC), commonly referred to as simply Fulvia, was an aristocratic Roman woman who lived during the Late Roman Republic. Through her mar
2 CONC riage to three of the most promising Roman men of her generation, Publius Clodius Pulcher, Gaius Scribonius Curio and Mark Antony, she gained access to power. 
2 CONT
2 CONT All three husbands were politically active populares, tribunes and supporters of Julius Caesar. Though she is more famous for her involvement in Antony's career, many scholars believe that she was politically active with all of he
2 CONC r husbands.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fulvia is remembered in the history of the late Roman Republic for her political ambition and activity. She is most famous for her activities during her third marriage and her involvement in the Perusine War of 41-40 BC. She was t
2 CONC he first Roman non-mythological woman to appear on Roman coins.
2 CONT
