2 CONC from the Isle of Man, and possibly the person named on an inscription ("CRUX GURIAT") on a cross in the Isle of Man which has been dated to the eighth or ninth century.4 He was nominally the King of Ynys Manaw (the Isle of Man) du
2 CONC ring the struggle against Norse and Danish settlement on the island.1 He was born circa 750 at Isle of Man, Wales.1 He was the son of Elidyr ap Sandde, Brenin Ynys Manau and Celemion verch Tudwal o Ynys Manau.1,3 Gwriad ab Elidyr,
2 CONC  Brenin Ynys Manau married Esyllt ferch Cynan Dindaethwy, daughter of Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri Molwynog, Brenin Gwynedd and Matilda of Flint, before 764.5 Gwriad ab Elidyr, Brenin Ynys Manau died in 825.2
