2 CONT The Senate was the most powerful institution of the Republic; they passedlaws, declared war and discussed all matters affecting the city. From itsmembers, two consuls were elected who would take care of Rome's executiveand militar
2 CONC y matters. The consuls had to be 42 years old and had to haveserved in other posts. They served for one year and each consul couldveto the edicts of the other.
