2 CONC , she appeared to have travelled with her father. In 36 BC, Antonia married Pythodoros of Tralles, who was an Anatolian Greek, who originated from Tralles (modern Aydın, Turkey). He was extremely wealthy and was a friend to the la
2 CONC te triumvir Pompey. Pythodoros was about 20 years older than Antonia.
