1 NOTE [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Sources: Young; Kraentzler 1747a, 1747b; History of Morgan Family.   Young: Merfyn Frych (the Freckled) married Nest, heiress of Powys.   History: King of Gwynedd 825. Extended the size of his kingdom. Married Nest, daughter of Ca
2 CONC dell ap Brochwel, King of Powys. Their children were Rhodri and Gwriad, who was killed with his brother in 878.   K: Mervyn Vrych, King of Manau Guotodin, North Britain. But gives different wife, Essylt or Isold. History of Morgan
2 CONC  Family says she is his mother, not wife.     Will have go get a third opinion on this and other difference.
2 CONT Merfyn Frych (the Freckled), was the king of Gwynedd, where his court was a centre of some culture and a meeting place of Irish scholars travelling to the Continent.  On the death, 825, of his mother's uncle, Hywel ap Rhodri Molwy
2 CONC nog, king of Gwynedd (last king in Anglesey of Cunedda's line), Merfyn became king in Anglesey; later, on the death of Hywel ap Caradoc, he appears to have acquired kingships of adjacent mainland cantrefs.  Thus were united the in
2 CONC heritances of last direct descendants in Gwynedd of Cunedda.  Merfyn married Nest, daughter of Cadell ap Brochwel of Powys, and died 844, leaving a son, Rhodri Mawr. [Source 1]
2 CONT King of Gwynedd 825.  Extended the size of his kingdom.  Married Nest, daughter of Cadel ap Brochwel, King of Powys.  Their children were Rhodri and Gwriad, who was killed with his brother in 878.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:  1.  Burke, Sir Bernard, C.B., LL.D, Ulster King of Arms.  _Landed Gentry_
2 CONT       (entry under Powell), page 577.
2 CONT   2.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.
