2 CONT =Messalla=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT (Lucius Valerius) Messalla (fl. 3rd century) was a Roman senator who was appointed consul in AD 280.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Messalla is assumed to be a member of the third century Patrician Gens Valeria, possibly the son of Lucius Valerius Poplicola Balbinus Maximus. In AD 280 he was appointed consul prior alongside Vettius Gratus.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been suggested that he had a son, Lucius Valerius Maximus Basilius, who was Praefectus Urbi of Rome in AD 319.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
