1 NOTE KNOWN AS "THE ELDER"; CONSUL 107 BC, AND 104-101 BC; 158 BC-86 BC
1 NOTE Gaius Marius var en fremragende general som sto bak flere reformer i den romerske hæren. Marius var også leder av Populares, en av fraksjonene i Senatet. Mot slutten av Marius' liv, i 86 f.kr., nådde de politiske stridighetene et 
2 CONC høydepunkt, og spliden mellom ham og hans nevø Lucius Cornelius Sulla førte til borgerkrig.
1 NOTE At the time of Caesar's birth, Gaius Marius was the most powerful man inRome. Though he was a new man (i.e., one without noble ancestors), he hadrisen to prominence through judicious alliances with the powerful Metelliclan and lat
2 CONC er marriage with Julia. His main claim to fame was thesuccessful conclusion of the Jugurthine war (104), and the defeat of theGermanic Teutones (102) and Cimbri (101). Marius was popularis, a termwhich seem to indicate an inclinat
2 CONC ion towards getting one's legislationratified directly through the People's Assembly.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was opposed by the optimates, a faction of the aristocracy whichbelieved that everything should be ratified in the Senate and who viewedthe popularis as revolutionaries. In 99, Marius helped put down the civilunrest instigated 
2 CONC by his former allies and fellow popularis, the tribuneSaturnius. When Saturnius and his henchmen were killed by an angry mob,Marius lost much of his earlier popularity, though he may have regainedmuch of it by 92, when Caesar's fa
2 CONC ther was elected praetor.
