2 CONT REFN: 6360Patrick Sims-Williams [in the article "Historical Need andLiterary Narrative: a Caveat from Ninth-Century Wales", Welsh HistoryReview, vol. 17 (1994), pp. 1-40] has recently argued (conclusively, inmy opinion) that neith
2 CONC er Nest nor Angharad ever existed, and that theywere inventions of later genealogists who wanted to give Rhodri's familya line of descent from the earlier kings of Powys and Ceredigion.[CusterFebruary 1, 2002 Family Tree.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT [merge G675.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Sims-Williams [in the article "Historical Need and LiteraryNarrative: a Caveat from Ninth-Century Wales", Welsh History Review, vol.17 (1994), pp. 1-40] has recently argued (conclusively, in my opinion)that neither Nest no
2 CONC r Angharad ever existed, and that they wereinventions of later genealogists who wanted to give Rhodri's family aline of descent from the earlier kings of Powys and Ceredigion.
1 NOTE 34th great grandmother
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Welsh: Merfyn; Latin: Marbinus; English: Mervin;
2 CONT
2 CONT Merfyn "The Freckled" was the 6th great grandson of Llywarch Hen and heir to the lost Kingdom of South Rheged. His father, Gwriad ap Elidyr, appears to have hailed from Ellan Fannin (Isle of Mann) which earlier ancestors had made 
2 CONC their home. His mother was Esyllt ferch Cynan, the heiress of Gwynedd, and after the death of her uncle in 825, the throne was secured for Merfyn. Merfyn brought a new stability as well as a new dynasty to Gwynedd after many years
2 CONC  of Civil War. He reigned for 19 years, and died in 844
1 NOTE [large-G675.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Sims-Williams [in the article "Historical Need and LiteraryNarrative: a Caveat from Ninth-Century Wales", Welsh History Review, vol.17 (1994), pp. 1-40] has recently argued (conclusively, in my opinion)that neither Nest no
2 CONC r Angharad ever existed, and that they wereinventions of later genealogists who wanted to give Rhodri's family aline of descent from the earlier kings of Powys and Ceredigion.
1 NOTE AFN: RKJR-5M & FJGT-Q7 are the same person with different husbands.  The Father and Mother AFN#'s are the same for both lines.
1 NOTE
2 CONT
