1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Gaius Porcius Cato=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaius Porcius Cato (1st Century BC) was a distant relative, probably a second cousin, of the more famous Marcus Porcius Cato, called Cato the Younger. This Cato was probably the son of Gaius Porcius Cato, the homonymous consul of 
2 CONC 114 BC, being then the grandson of Marcus Porcius Cato Licinianus and thereby the Great-grandson of the famous Cato the Censor, often called Cato the Elder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaius Porcius Cato was a client (an adherent) of triumvir Marcus Licinius Crassus and was an ally of Clodius (Publius Clodius Pulcher) the infamous Patrician tribune of the plebs, in his street gang war against Milo (Titus Annius 
2 CONC Milo). He attacked Publius Cornelius Lentulus Spinther and Gnaeus Pompeius Magnus (Pompey the Great) in 59 BC by prosecuting a follower, Gabinius for ambitus (political corruption) but was thwarted by a Pompean praetor and was cha
2 CONC sed from the rostra by an angry crowd. In 57 BC he spoke against delaying the aedelician elections (Clodius was standing and Milo wanted the delay to allow a prosecution).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaius_Porcius_Cato_(tribune)
