2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~summer/Owen.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri (854–909) was the son of Rhodri Mawr ("the Great"). He inherited the kingdom of Seisyllwg from his father in 878, and passed it to his son, Hywel Dda ("the Good"), on his death in 909. Cadell and Hywel had previou
2 CONC sly conquered Dyfed in 904/905, establishing Hywel as the king in that region. After his father's death, Hywel merged the two kingdoms to establish Deheubarth.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Cadell ap Rhodri   
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadell was born about 0861 in Deheubarth, Wales.1   Cadell's father was Rhodri (Mawr, The Great) ap Merfyn and his mother was Angharad verch Meurig.  His paternal grandparents were Merfyn (The Freckled) Frych ap Gwriad and Nest ve
2 CONC rch Cadell; his maternal grandparents were Meurig ap Dyfnwallon and <Unknown>. He had eight brothers and two sisters, named Anarawd, Merfyn, Aeddan, Tudwal, Meurig, Rhodri, Gwriad, Gwyddelig, Nest and Angharad.  He was the third o
2 CONC ldest of the eleven children.  He died in 0909.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadell, the 2nd son of Rhodri Mawr, succeeded to the Kingdom of South Wales, which was called Deheubarth, their residence being Dynevor or Dmasvawr, the Great Palace. The fatal policy of Roderick in dividing his dominions soon bec
2 CONC ame apparent from the conduct of his sons. For in 892/3 we find Anarawd uniting with the English against his brother Cadell; when they invaded his territory and devastated the country of Cardigan and the vale of Towy. And again we
2 CONC  find Cadell, Prince of South Wales, taking forcible possession of Powis on the death of his brother Mervyn in 901. Cadell died in 907, leaving three sons: Howell Dha, i. e., Howell, the Good, Meyric and Clydawc, of whom the latte
2 CONC r was killed by his brother Meyric about 917. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Kin of Mellcene Thurman Smith, page 800) 
2 CONT
2 CONT CADELH who became Prince of South Wales 877; took Powys from his brother Merfyn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Fenwick Allied Ancestry, page 181)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Cadell ap Rhodri & Rheingar 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had three sons named The Good, Meurig and Clydog.
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal Details
2 CONT
2 CONT  Cadell ap Rhodri
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadell was born about 0861 in Deheubarth, Wales.1   He died in 0909.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Rheingar
2 CONT
2 CONT Rheingar was born about 0865 in Carmarthenshire, Wales.1   Rheingar is no longer alive.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT   Hywel (The Good) ap Cadell
2 CONT
2 CONT Hywel, known as The Good, was born about 0880.1   He died in 0950.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Meurig ap Cadell
2 CONT
2 CONT Meurig was born about 0889.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Clydog ap Cadell
2 CONT
2 CONT Clydog was born about 0891.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  878-909    	 Reign
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: CADELL. In the division of the dominion of his father he was given Deheubarth and a large part of South Wales. His brother Merfyn received Powys. He and his brothers made so much trouble for the neighboring kingdoms tha
2 CONC t they were compelled to seek help from Alfred the Great. In 893 he was attacked by his brother Anarawd, King of Gwynedd, who invaded and plundered Seisyllwg. After the death of his brother Merfyn, Cadell drove out his nephews and
2 CONC  appropriated Powys to himself. He died about 909 and his kingdom was divided between his sons, Hywel and Clydog. In the Mostyn Manuscript No. 117 the pedigree of his distinguished descendant, Llewelyn ap Gruffyd, is traced back t
2 CONC hrough Cadell to "Adam, Son of God." If the compiler did not draw on his imagination for parts of this pedigree he must have had access to records not now in existence. [Source: The Weaver Genealogy, p 44] 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri (854–909) was the son of Rhodri Mawr ("the Great"). He inherited the kingdom of Seisyllwg from his father in 878, and passed it to his son, Hywel Dda ("the Good"), on his death in 909. Cadell and Hywel had previou
2 CONC sly conquered Dyfed in 904/905, establishing Hywel as the king in that region. After his father's death, Hywel merged the two kingdoms to establish Deheubarth.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri (854–909) was the son of Rhodri Mawr ("the Great"). He inherited the kingdom of Seisyllwg from his father in 878, and passed it to his son, Hywel Dda ("the Good"), on his death in 909. Cadell and Hywel had previou
2 CONC sly conquered Dyfed in 904/905, establishing Hywel as the king in that region. After his father's death, Hywel merged the two kingdoms to establish Deheubarth.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Cadell Ap Rhodri Mawr King Of South Wales 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 861 in Deheubarth, Wales 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: ABT 910 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Rhodri Mawr Ap Merfyn b: ABT 809 in Caer Seiont, Carnarvonshire, Wales 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Angharad Verch Meurig b: ABT 825 in Ceredigion, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Rheingar Of Dehelibarth b: ABT 865 in Carmarthenshire, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT  Hywel 'Dda' Ap Cadell b: ABT 887 in Deheubarth, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri, was the son of Rhodri Mawr ("the Great"). He inherited the kingdom of Seisyllwg from his father in 878, and passed it to his son, Hywel Dda ("the Good"), on his death in 909. Cadell and Hywel had previously conqu
2 CONC ered Dyfed in 904/905, establishing Hywel as the king in that region. After his father's death, Hywel merged the two kingdoms to establish Deheubarth.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri inherited the kingdom of Seisyllwg from his father in 878, and passed it to his son, Hywel Dda ("the Good"), on his death in 909. Cadell and Hywel had previously conquered Dyfed in 904/905, establishing Hywel as t
2 CONC he king in that region. After his father's death, Hywel merged the two kingdoms to establish Deheubarth.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT RHODRI MAWR had unified the greater part of Wales, and his two sons who shared the rule founded medieval dynasties, ANARAWD of the house of Aberffraw in the north of Wales, and CADELL of the house of Dinefwr in the south.
2 CONT
2 CONT CADELL and his brother had taken over Dyfed (roughly equivalent to modern Pembrokeshire), and he held it with Cardiganshire and Carmarthenshire as one unit known as Deheubarth (“the southern part”). It covered the whole of south w
2 CONC est Wales (Maund p.45), and seven centuries later our LEIGH and NASH families lived there. CADELL also apparently asked for and received the support of king Alfred of Wessex, who having just defeated the Norsemen and united much o
2 CONC f England, enjoyed great renown and power. This Welsh desire for support by Alfred was later construed as homage and acceptance by the Welsh kings that Alfred was overlord of Wales. As such, in later years homage was regularly dem
2 CONC anded from all Welsh princes by the English crown. It played a crucial role for centuries in the political history of Wales and England and became a major factor in the unsuccessful Welsh effort to retain their independent kingdom
2 CONC  (J.Davies p.85). The life of CADELL’S son, the next great king of Wales HYWEL DDA, who was given his unique epithet, the Good, by his descendants.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ancestor of the Sovereigns of South Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT Courtesy of fantastically full family tree cf.:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hughes of Gwerclas 1/2/3/4:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_2.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_3.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_4.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri (854–909) was King of Seisyllwg, a minor kingdom in southwestern Wales, from about 872 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadell was the second son of Rhodri the Great of Gwynedd and Angharad, a princess from Seisyllwg. In 872 Angharad's brother Gwgon, King of Seisyllwg, drowned without leaving an heir. Rhodri became steward over the kingdom, and whi
2 CONC le he was unable to make a legal claim to the throne, he was able to install Cadell as king.[1] He passed it to his son, Hywel Dda, at his death in 909. Cadell and Hywel together also conquered Dyfed in 904–905, establishing Hywel
2 CONC  as the king in that region. After his father's death, Hywel ruled the kingdoms jointly as Deheubarth.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The wife of Cadell is unknown.  (See http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WALES.htm)
