2 CONT =Titus Junius Brutus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Titus Junius Brutus (died c. 509 BCE) was the elder son of Lucius Junius Brutus, who was one of Rome's first two consuls in 509 BC. His mother was Vitellia.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the invitation of his uncles, called Vitellii, he and his younger brother Tiberius Junius Brutus joined the Tarquinian conspiracy. When the conspiracy was discovered, he and the other conspirators were executed by order of the 
2 CONC consuls. Punishment was carried out by the lictors, and included being stripped naked, beaten with rods and then beheaded. Lucius Junius Brutus was admired for his strong stance in ordering the execution of his sons, although at t
2 CONC imes during the execution he showed his emotions.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
