2 CONT
2 CONT Owain ap Hywel (died c. 930) was a king of Glywysing and Gwent in southeastern Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT Owain's father Hywel was king of Glywysing until his death around AD 886. Although the unified kingdom of Glywysing and Gwent became known as Morgannwg in honor of Owain's son Morgan the Old, Charles-Edwards argues that it is prob
2 CONC able that the two realms were already united during Owain's reign. Owain or his brother Arthfael must have gained control of Gwent by conquest or inheritance from the previous rulers (their cousins), with the realm becoming united
2 CONC  after Arthfael's death around 916.
2 CONT
2 CONT Along with Hywel the Good, Owain met with King Æthelstan of Wessex following the latter's conquest of Northumbria. Around 927, he and Hywel "established peace with pledge and oaths" at Eamont Bridge near Penrith. The subsequent tr
2 CONC ibute payments in silver and in kind were bemoaned by the bards as a heavy burden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Owain's death initially divided the kingdom again among his three sons, but the long-lived Morgan outlasted his brothers and reunited the realm again, which thenceforth carried his name.
2 CONT
2 CONT See https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owain_ap_Hywel_(Glywysing)
