2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Idwal Foel ap Anarawd (Idwal the Bald) (died 942) was a King of Gwynedd, also called King of the Britons by William of Malmesbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT Idwal inherited the throne of Gwynedd on the death of his father, Anarawd ap Rhodri in 916. He was obliged to acknowledge Athelstan of England as overlord. Following the death of Athelstan, Idwal and his brother Elisedd took to ar
2 CONC ms against the English, but both were killed in battle in 942. The rule of Gwynedd should now have passed to his sons, Iago ab Idwal and Idwal, usually called Ieuaf ab Idwal. However Hywel Dda, already ruler of most of south Wales
2 CONC , invaded Gwynedd and forced them into exile, adding Gwynedd to his realm. After Howell's death in 950, Idwal's sons were able to claim the kingdom.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idwal_Foel
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Killed in battle with the Saxons.
