2 CONC , where he ruled for nearly 40 years, paid tribute of 300 wolves' heads to Edgar, King of England, 962; tried to recover the throne of Gwynedd, and died 988, having had a son, Einion ap Owain. [Source 1]
2 CONT "Descended on his mother's side from Votiporix, the third century Irish invader of South Wales.  Married Angharad, Queen of Powys, to settle clains of her father Llewelyn to the throne of Powys.  Had sons Cadwallon, who became Kin
2 CONC g of South Wales, and Einion."  King of South Wales, 950. [Source 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad and her husband were second cousins. [Source 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:  1.  Burke, Sir Bernard, C.B., LL.D., Ulster King of Arms.  _Landed Gentry_
2 CONT       (entry under Powell), page 577.
2 CONT   2.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.  3.  Bartrum, Peter C.  _Welsh Genealogies, AD 300-1400_.  University of
2 CONT       Wales Press, 1978; page 42.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Sources: Dictionary of National Biography; AF.   Dictionary: Owain was a descendant of Hywel Dda, who "had been a vigorous ruler over Gwynedd."
2 CONT Owain ap Hywel Dda, king of Deheubarth, where he ruled for nearly 40 years, paid tribute of 300 wolves' heads to Edgar, King of England, 962; tried to recover the throne of Gwynedd, and died 988, having had a son, Einion ap Owain.
2 CONC  [Source 1]
2 CONT "Descended on his mother's side from Votiporix, the third century Irish invader of South Wales.  Married Angharad, Queen of Powys, to settle clains of her father Llewelyn to the throne of Powys.  Had sons Cadwallon, who became Kin
2 CONC g of South Wales, and Einion."  King of South Wales, 950. [Source 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad and her husband were second cousins. [Source 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:  1.  Burke, Sir Bernard, C.B., LL.D., Ulster King of Arms.  _Landed Gentry_
2 CONT       (entry under Powell), page 577.
2 CONT   2.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.  3.  Bartrum, Peter C.  _Welsh Genealogies, AD 300-1400_.  University of
2 CONT       Wales Press, 1978; page 42.
1 NOTE KING OF GLAMORGAN
1 NOTE Owain was the prince of South Wales.  He shared the sovereignty of North, 
2 CONT South, and Middle Wales with his father and his two brothers, Rodri and 
2 CONT Edwain.
2 CONT At their death he took over rule of all, but the sons of Idwal Voel took 
2 CONT from him North and Middle Wales.  He maintained the independence of South 
2 CONT Wales for
2 CONT 32 years, dieing in 986, full of years and honor.
1 NOTE PRINCE (OR KING) OF SOUTH WALES 954-988; UPON MARRIAGE BECAME KING OF POWYS
