2 CONT C. 983, he banded with the Anglo-Saxons, forging an alliance with Aelthere of Mercia, in order to defeat Einion ab Owain, at that time the ruler of Dyfed.  Later, however, he would be slain "through the treachery of the Saxons."  
2 CONC (See Thomas Jones's translation of Peniarth MS 70 (16).)
