1 NOTE Maredudd ap Owain
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=1fa14e22-7018-475f-a5e7-649805fa0cdc&tid=9784512&pid=-634508819
1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT REFN: 6352
1 NOTE The son of Owain ap Hywel Dda, whom he succeeded as sole ruler of Deheubarth in 986, three elder brothers having already predeceased their fathe
2 CONT In the same year he reunited Gwynedd to Deheubarth.  He exercised strong leadership against the Saxons and the Danes.  His only son Cadwallon, died in 992 and Maredudd was succeeded on his death in 999 by Llywelyn ap Seisyll, the 
2 CONC husband of his daughter Angharad Ferch Maredudd.
1 NOTE Annales Cambriae page 95 of History of Wales
1 NOTE OR "MAREDUDD"; PRINCE OF POWYS; KING OF WALES 986-999
