2 CONT =Arruns Tarquinius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Arruns Tarquinius L. f. L. n. was the second son of Lucius Tarquinius Superbus, the seventh and last King of Rome.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''History'''
2 CONT
2 CONT During his father's reign, he accompanied his elder brother, Titus, and their cousin, Lucius Junius Brutus, to consult the Oracle at Delphi regarding an omen witnessed by the king. After she had interpreted the omen, the princes a
2 CONC sked the Oracle who should succeed their father as king; her reply was that he who should first kiss his mother upon their return would succeed the king. While Titus and Arruns assumed that this meant their actual mother, Brutus c
2 CONC orrectly intuited that mother earth was intended, and so deliberately stumbled and fell upon the trio's return to Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the overthrow of the monarchy in 509 BC, Titus and Arruns went with their father to Caere, while Brutus was elected one of the first consuls. After the first unsuccessful attempt by the Tarquins to regain the throne in 5
2 CONC 09, Arruns commanded the Etruscan cavalry at the Battle of Silva Arsia. Having spied from afar the lictors, and thereby recognising the presence of a consul, Arruns soon saw that his cousin Brutus was in command of the Roman caval
2 CONC ry. The two men charged each other, and were each speared to death. The battle ended in a Roman victory, and the Tarquins remained in exile.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arruns_Tarquinius_(son_of_Tarquin_the_Proud)
