2 CONT =Titus Tarquinius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Titus was the eldest son of Lucius Tarquinius Superbus, the last king of Rome. During his father's reign, he accompanied his younger brother Aruns and his cousin Lucius Junius Brutus to consult the Oracle at Delphi to have interpr
2 CONC eted an omen witnessed by the king.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 509 BC, upon the overthrow of the monarchy, Titus went into exile at Caere with his father and his brother Aruns.
2 CONT
2 CONT In around 496 BC he fought with his father and the Latins against Rome at the Battle of Lake Regillus. During the battle, Marcus Valerius Volusus, who had been the Roman consul in 505 BC, charged Titus in an attempt to slay him, b
2 CONC ut was himself killed by Titus' men.
2 CONT
