2 CONT LDS
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born about 965AD, of Maelor Gymraeg, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT He is NOT the Rhiwallon who married Lettice (Letita) {S6}, but that was a later Rhiwallon who was born about 1130. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is confused with Rhiwallon ap Cynfyn, Prince of Powys, who was killed in 1069 at the Battle of Mechain in Montgomeryshire, Wales. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was known as Rhiwallon ap Dyngad of Maelor Gymraeg. Maelor is a border area of north-east Wales. It originated as a Cantref of the Kingdom of Powys, focused on Bangor-on-Dee. The Maelor was first divided from the rest of Wales 
2 CONC by the construction of Offa's Dyke in the eighth century, but was reclaimed for Wales during the reign of Stephen of England (1135-54) by Madog ap Maredudd of Powys. The Maelor Gymraeg, the "Welsh-speaking Maelor", is an ancient d
2 CONC istrict of Wales to the west of the River Dee, and corresponds approximately to the later parishes of Bersham, Erbistock, Marchwiel, Ruabon and Wrexham in the historic county of Denbighshire which was created in 1536. The Maelor G
2 CONC ymraeg is separate from The Maelor Saesneg, the "English-speaking Maelor," an area of Wales along the eastern border that merged with Cheshire.
