2 CONT --------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  Angharad verch Maredudd   
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad was born about 0982 in Rhuddlan, Wales.1  Birth Notes Angharad's father was Maredydd ap Owain and her mother was <Unknown>.  Her paternal grandparents were Owain ap Hywel and Angharad verch Llewelyn. She had two brothers 
2 CONC and a sister, named Rhys, Cadwallon and Lleucu.  She was the youngest of the four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Llywelyn ap Seisyllt & Angharad verch Maredudd 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had a son named Gruffudd.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gruffudd ap Llewellen Gruffudd was born about 1000 in Rhuddlan, Flintshire, Wales.1   He died on August 5th, 1063.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1018 Llywelyn ap Seisyll killed Aeddan ab Blegywryd and his four sons. Quite who Aeddan was is open to speculation, but Llywelyn was probably king of Gwynedd - he certainly was four years later. Llywelyn's background is obscure
2 CONC . Medieval genealogists contrived to make his mother (Prawst) the daughter of an otherwise unknown son (Elisedd) of Anarawd ap Rhodri Mawr. It is not unreasonable to assume that both Prawst and Elisedd are inventions. From the 'Br
2 CONC ut y Tywysogion', it is known that Llywelyn married Angharad, daughter of Maredudd ab Owain. In 1022, an Irishman called Rhain, claiming to be the son of Maredudd, gained acceptance as king of Deheubarth:
2 CONT
2 CONT "And Llywelyn, son of Seisyll, supreme king of Gwynedd, and the chief and most renowned king of all the Britons, made war against him." 'Brut y Tywysogion' Rhain was defeated, at Abergwili - he fled, never to be seen again. Llywel
2 CONC yn followed up his victory by ravaging Deheubarth ("destroying it as far as Mercia").
2 CONT
2 CONT *Angharad verch Maredydd Queen of Powys born about 0982 Deheubarth, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT father:
2 CONT *Maredydd ap Owain born about 0938 Dynevor Castle, Carmarthshire, Wales died 0999
2 CONT
2 CONT mother: unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT siblings:
2 CONT *Lleucu verch Maredudd born about 0972 Deheubarth, Wales Rhys ap Maredudd born about 0963 Deheubarth, Wales Cadwallon ap Maredudd born about 0966 Deheubarth, Wales died 0992
2 CONT
2 CONT spouse (1st):
2 CONT *Llywelyn ap Seisyllt King of Gwynedd & Deheubarth born about 0980 Rhuddlan, Flintshire, Wales died 1021/23 married about 1010
2 CONT
2 CONT children (from 1st marriage):
2 CONT *Gruffydd ap Llewelyn King of Gwynedd & Powys born about 1011 Rhuddlan, Flintshire, Wales died 5 August 1063
2 CONT
2 CONT spouse (2nd):
2 CONT *Cynfyn ap Gwerystan King of Powys born about 1002 Powys, Wales married 1023
2 CONT
2 CONT children (from 2nd marriage):
2 CONT *Bleddyn ap Cynfyn born about 1025 Montgomeryshire, Wales died 1075
2 CONT *Miss verch Cynfyn born about 1024 Of Powys, Wales
2 CONT *Rhiwallon ap Cynfyn born about 1025 Powys, Wales died 1070 (slain) Battle Mechain, Montgomeryshire, Wales
2 CONT *Iwerydd verch Cynfyn born about 1024 Powys, Wales
2 CONT *Nest verch Cynfyn born about 1027 Powys, Wales Gwerydd verch Cynfyn
2 CONT
2 CONT biographical and/or anecdotal:
2 CONT
2 CONT notes or source: LDS
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Angharad married first to Llywelyn ap Seisyll, Prince of Deheubarth (1018 - 1023) and they had a son: Gruffydd ap Llywelyn who inflicted a series of defeats on the English, and made alliances with the enemies of King Edward the Co
2 CONC nfessor.  Gruffydd fought a long campaign against rival kings to win overall control of Wales.  By 1055, he had become master of Deheubarth and had expanded his rule to the lesser kingdoms of Morgannwg (Glamorgan) and Gwent.  In 1
2 CONC 063, Earl Harold Godwinsson (later Harold II) and his brother Tostig made a joint attack on Gwynedd.  At the same time, Deheubarth rebelled against Gruffydd’s rule.  Gruffydd fled and was murdered by his own men. Gruffydd married 
2 CONC Ealdgyth, a daughter of Ælfgar, Earl of Mercia. Ealdgyth married second in circa 1064 to Harold Godwineson, the last Anglo-Saxon King of England. Ealdgyth and Gruffydd had a son: Maredudd ap Gruffydd who was excluded from the thro
2 CONC ne by his uncles Bleddyn ap Cynfyn and Rhywallon ap Cynfyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad married second to Cynfyn ap Gwerystan of Powys, a lord in Powys about whom little is known. Angharad and Cynfyn had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhywallon ap Cynfyn Bleddyn ap Cynfyn a daughter who married Owain ap Edwin, Lord Tegaingl, and they had a daughter: Angharad who married Gruffydd ap Cynan, Prince of Gwynedd and/or King of North Wales from 1081 until his death in
2 CONC  1137.  Click on Gruffydd ap Cynan for this line.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://www.robertsewell.ca/powys.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT daughter of Maredudd ab Owain, wife of Llywelyn ap Seisyll, King of Gwynedd and of Deheubarth, with her first husband, and mother of Bleddyn ap Cynfyn with her second husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Angharad verch Maredudd Angharad was born about 0982 in Rhuddlan, Wales.1 Birth Notes Angharad's father was Maredydd ap Owain and her mother was <Unknown>. Her paternal grandparents were Owain ap Hywel and Angharad verch Llewelyn.
2 CONC  She had two brothers and a sister, named Rhys, Cadwallon and Lleucu. She was the youngest of the four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Llywelyn ap Seisyllt & Angharad verch Maredudd They had a son named Gruffudd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gruffudd ap Llewellen Gruffudd was born about 1000 in Rhuddlan, Flintshire, Wales.1 He died on August 5th, 1063.1
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1018 Llywelyn ap Seisyll killed Aeddan ab Blegywryd and his four sons. Quite who Aeddan was is open to speculation, but Llywelyn was probably king of Gwynedd - he certainly was four years later. Llywelyn's background is obscure
2 CONC . Medieval genealogists contrived to make his mother (Prawst) the daughter of an otherwise unknown son (Elisedd) of Anarawd ap Rhodri Mawr. It is not unreasonable to assume that both Prawst and Elisedd are inventions. From the 'Br
2 CONC ut y Tywysogion', it is known that Llywelyn married Angharad, daughter of Maredudd ab Owain. In 1022, an Irishman called Rhain, claiming to be the son of Maredudd, gained acceptance as king of Deheubarth:
2 CONT
2 CONT "And Llywelyn, son of Seisyll, supreme king of Gwynedd, and the chief and most renowned king of all the Britons, made war against him." 'Brut y Tywysogion' Rhain was defeated, at Abergwili - he fled, never to be seen again. Llywel
2 CONC yn followed up his victory by ravaging Deheubarth ("destroying it as far as Mercia").
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad verch Maredydd Queen of Powys born about 0982 Deheubarth, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT father:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maredydd ap Owain born about 0938 Dynevor Castle, Carmarthshire, Wales died 0999
2 CONT
2 CONT mother: unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lleucu verch Maredudd born about 0972 Deheubarth, Wales Rhys ap Maredudd born about 0963 Deheubarth, Wales Cadwallon ap Maredudd born about 0966 Deheubarth, Wales died 0992
2 CONT
2 CONT spouse (1st):
2 CONT
2 CONT Llywelyn ap Seisyllt King of Gwynedd & Deheubarth born about 0980 Rhuddlan, Flintshire, Wales died 1021/23 married about 1010
2 CONT
2 CONT children (from 1st marriage):
2 CONT
2 CONT Gruffydd ap Llewelyn King of Gwynedd & Powys born about 1011 Rhuddlan, Flintshire, Wales died 5 August 1063 spouse (2nd):
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynfyn ap Gwerystan King of Powys born about 1002 Powys, Wales married 1023
2 CONT
2 CONT children (from 2nd marriage):
2 CONT
2 CONT Bleddyn ap Cynfyn born about 1025 Montgomeryshire, Wales died 1075 Miss verch Cynfyn born about 1024 Of Powys, Wales Rhiwallon ap Cynfyn born about 1025 Powys, Wales died 1070 (slain) Battle Mechain, Montgomeryshire, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT Iwerydd verch Cynfyn born about 1024 Powys, Wales Nest verch Cynfyn born about 1027 Powys, Wales Gwerydd verch Cynfyn
2 CONT
