2 CONT '''Tiberius Aemilius Mamercus''' or was a Roman senator active in the fifth century BC. He was consul in 470 and 467 BC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mamercus was a member of the Aemilii Mamerci, a branch of the gens Aemilia. '''He was the son of Lucius Aemilius Mamercus, consul in 484, 478, and 473, and the grandson of a Mamercus Aemilius.'''[2] 
2 CONT
