1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lord of Ial and Ystrad Alun
2 CONT
2 CONT At 14, he went to serve in the court of Llewelyn ap Seisyll, and remained there after the death of the king (1023).  He married Efa verch Cynfyn c 1033.  Later, he became Gruffudd ap Llewelyn's penteleu, or battle leader, at which
2 CONC  point he began to wear the gold torque of the battle leader; hence his nickname, "Aurdorchog."  For this service, he was granted Ial, south of Ystrad Alun.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173393063941 (February 5, 2023; Anne Brannen, curator)
