1 NAME Arruns Tarquinius
2 GIVN Arruns Tarquinius
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Arruns Tarquinius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Arruns Tarquinius was the younger son of Demaratus of Corinth, who migrated to the Etruscan city of Tarquinii in the 7th century. He died shortly before his father, leaving his wife pregnant. When Demaratus died, he left no inheri
2 CONC tance for his grandson, also named Arruns, who was thus born into poverty, although Demaratus had been wealthy. The child came to be called Egerius, meaning "the needy one."
2 CONT
2 CONT Demaratus' elder son, Lucius, migrated to Rome, where he eventually rose to the throne as Lucius Tarquinius. After subduing the Latin town of Collatia, Tarquin placed his nephew in charge of the Roman garrison there. Egerius was t
2 CONC he father of Lucius Tarquinius Collatinus, one of the first Roman consuls in 509 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arruns_Tarquinius_(son_of_Demaratus)
