1 NOTE Harold, still in his early twenties, met and fell in love with Edith Swan Neck, who he met in Nazeing in Essex. She became his loyal mistress and he would visit her whenever he could. Harold suffered paralysis soon after their mee
2 CONC ting, but managed to recover. To give thanks to God, he built an abbey at Waltham Cross. He would later be laid to rest there after his final battle.
