1 NOTE Maredudd joined in the revolt of his brothers Cadwgan and Iorwerth in1102, but failed to change sides when they did and was handed over to theEnglish. He escaped in 1107 and worked with his nephew, Owain. On Owain'sdeath in 1116, 
2 CONC Maredudd succeeded. In 1122 his raids across the Englishborder antagonized Henry I "Longshanks", who led an expedition againsthim. He was reduced to taking refuge in Snowdonia before making peace onterms.
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded to the thrown in 1116 AD.
