1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/6516/TABLES%20-%20EARLY%20SERIES_42.png?sequence=13&isAllowed=y (May 27, 2018; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his brother Maredudd as king of Deheubarth in 1072, and in 1075 was part of the killing of Bleddyn ap Cynfyn.  In 1078 Trahaearn ap Caradog defeated him in battle; he was later killed by Caradog ap Gruffudd at the bat
2 CONC tle of Mynydd Carn.
2 CONT
