1 NAME Arruns Tarquinius Egerius
2 GIVN Arruns Tarquinius Egerius
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Arruns Tarquinius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Arruns Tarquinius, commonly called Egerius, was a member of the royal family of early Rome.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was Arruns Tarquinius, son of Demaratus of Corinth. Demaratus had settled at Tarquinii during the seventh century BC, and married an Etruscan noblewoman. They had two sons, Lucius and Arruns. Arruns died shortly before 
2 CONC his father, leaving his wife pregnant. Not knowing of his grandson, Demaratus left him no inheritance, and so Arruns was born into poverty despite his grandfather's wealth. For this reason, the child was called Egerius, meaning "t
2 CONC he needy one."
2 CONT
2 CONT At the urging of his wife, Tanaquil, Lucius Tarquinius migrated to Rome, where he found favour with the king, Ancus Marcius. Ultimately, Tarquin succeeded Marcius as the fifth King of Rome. After subduing the Latin town of Collati
2 CONC a, Tarquin placed his nephew in command of the Roman garrison there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arruns' son was Lucius Tarquinius Collatinus, one of the first Roman consuls in 509 BC. The rape of Collatinus' wife, Lucretia, by his cousin, Sextus Tarquinius, was the event that sparked the expulsion of the Roman kings. Ironica
2 CONC lly, public hatred of the Tarquins led Collatinus himself to resign the consulship and go into exile.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
