2 CONT Sources differ as to the wife of Rhys, therefore both are listed.
1 NOTE Rhys was the eldest son of the first Tedwr and spent the greatest portion 
2 CONT of his life in Brittany  though the rightful prince of South Wales.  He 
2 CONT was a leader of armies for more than 75 years.  Rhys returned from 
2 CONT Brittany when an old man to claim the sovereignty of South Wales, where he 
2 CONT was received with great acclaim by the people as Prince.  He was slain in 
2 CONT battle by the Normans in 1093 at the age of 96.
1 NOTE [large-G675.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources differ as to the wife of Rhys, therefore both are listed.
