2 CONT Cuhelyn's two sons Gwrwared and Llywelyn were powerful enough to force the Norman lord of Cemais to grant the pasturage of the commons of the Presely hills to them and their heirs, to be held to the use of the commoners of the lor
2 CONC dship, and afterwards confirmed "to the heirs of Gwrwared and Llewelyn sons of Cuhelyn"
