2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gruffydd_ap_Llywelyn#Marriage_and_issue '''source''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably as a consequence of his rapid rise in the marches, Bernard attracted the attention of Osbern fitz Richard, who gave him his daughter, Agnes (Nest), whose mother was the Welsh princess Nest, daughter of Gruffydd ap Llywely
2 CONC n and Edith of Mercia,[3] in marriage sometime before 1099.[9] She brought with her a dowry of Berrington and Little Hereford. (from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernard_de_Neufmarché '''another wiki-entry'''] )
2 CONT
