1 NOTE Rhys was the eldest son of Gruffydd, and was Prince of South Wales upon 
2 CONT the death of his father.  He was as great as any prince South Wales had 
2 CONT ever had.  The Normans refused him the name of prince on the theory that 
2 CONT Wales was a conquered country and had no longer a prince.  He was known as 
2 CONT "The Powerful Lord Rhys."
