2 CONT Certain medieval pedigrees [Peniarth Ms 176, pp 240; Harliean Ms 2299] claim Owain and Meurig had a third brother, Rhiryd Foel. But the wife and daughter assigned to him date his birth to c. 1155 and so he was more likely the son 
2 CONC of Meurig. Certainly he was not included among the named nephews of Madog who were given Cyfeiliog in 1149:  Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Brief Life of Gruffudd ap Maredudd; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id81.html. (Steven
2 CONC  Ferry, July 25, 2020.)
