2 CONT
2 CONT ************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Ranulf de Gernon, 2nd Earl of Chester and Maud FitzRobert, Countess of Chester. Not to be confused with her niece Beatrix (daughter of Hugh de Kevelioc).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Eynion de Tilston (born c. 1126)''' was a Norman knight and first lord of the manor of Tilston in the English county of Cheshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 12th century, William de Malpas gave Eynion the manor of Tilston in Cheshire, near the Welsh border. Sir Eynion was given the Manor of Tilston by the Earl of Chester in return for military service. The man who gave Sir Eyni
2 CONC on de Tilston the manor was William de Malpas. He and his descendents had to be constantly alert because of the Welsh who constantly raided the border areas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage,family and descendants[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1154 he married Beatrix de Gernons. Beatrix de Gernons was the daughter of Ranulf de Gernon, Earl of Chester.'''  They had at least one son born around 1156. The name of his son is unknown. - http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyn
2 CONC ion_de_Tilston Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Yet another  source lists her married to her son!  See the attached source document  for her name and ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ralph ap Einion ap Dafydd ap Sir William, born c. 1125, married '''Beatrix''', born c. 1135, a daughter of Ranulf de Gernon, 4th Earl of Chester, and sister of Hugh Cyfeiliog.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their daughter Beannan (born about 1160) married William ap Richard ap William lll ap William ll ap Sir William; their child David (b abt 1185) was Dan David "the clerk.". Beannan was not an heiress, her brother David inherited a 
2 CONC share of the moeity of Malpas.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * [http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id152.html THE "MALPAS" FAMILY IN CHESHIRE] By Darrell Wolcott     
2 CONT **Einion, born about 1090, was the son of David, born about 1060,  a younger brother of William II ap Sir William. Einion was the father of Ralph of Malpas, born about 1125, who married Beatrix, sister of Earl Hugh Cyfeiliog, 5th 
2 CONC Earl of Chester.
2 CONT **(d) William married Beannan, daughter of Ralph ap Einion ap David ap Sir William by Beatrix daughter of Earl Ranulf II of Chester, sister of Hugh Cyfeiliog
2 CONT ** (a) Pedigrees identify him as holding a moiety of Malpas, or one-half.  He would have inheirited 1/3 from his mother, being Ralph's part, and 1/6 from his father, being half of William II's part.  His brother, William III held 
2 CONC the other 1/6, which descended to Dan David.  The final 1/3 of Malpas was held by the line descended from David of 1060.  The daughter of Ralph shown in our chart, was not an heiress; she had a brother named David who inherited th
2 CONC e final 1/3.
2 CONT * [http://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000028955157936& "magaretdemaples.jpg"
2 CONT **Beatrix de Meschines m Ralph ap Eynion, lord of Malpas. Their daughter Margaret married David le Clerke de Malpas
