2 CONT First name aka 'Miles'/'Milon'.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: The book, 'The Thomas Book'
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Miles de Gloucester, 1st Earl of Hereford, Lord of Brecknock was the son of Walter de Gloucester, who appears as sheriff of that county between 1104 and 1121.
2 CONT
2 CONT Milo or Miles succeeded his father about the latter year.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was high in the service of Henry I between 1130 and 1135, he was Constable of England and combined the hereditary office of Sheriff of Gloucester with that of local justiciar for Gloucestershire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Miles founded Llanthony Secunda Priory, Gloucester, in 1136.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1141, he was rewarded with the earldom of Hereford when Matilda ruled the country. He remained loyal to the Empress after her defeat at Winchester the same year. John of Salisbury classes him with Geoffrey de Mandeville and oth
2 CONC ers who were non tam comites regni quam hostes publici. The charge is justified by his public policy; but the materials for appraising his personal character do not exist.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miles_de_Gloucester,_1st_Earl_of_Hereford
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Miles de Gloucester (Miles FitzWalter) was born on 1100.  Miles married Sybile De Neufmarche and had a child:  Bertha De Pitres.  He passed away on December 24, 1143.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE:  See link for further information :
2 CONT
