2 CONT Arnaud-Bellee, 1978: Milo of Gloucester (Milon, Miles Fitz Walter)inherited the title of constable of England and later that of earl ofHereford. He was the grandson of Roger de Pîtres, contemporary of Williamthe Conqueror and sher
2 CONC iff of Gloucester, and the son of Walter (Gautier),constable of Henry I. Milo possessed a considerable honor from theinheritance of his father's lands in Gloucestershire and his marriage in1121 to Sybyl, sole heiress of Bernard de
2 CONC  Newmarch. Milo died of ahunting accident on 25 December 1143, leaving four sons: Roger, who diedchildless in 1155; Walter, Henry, and Mahel, who all died childlessbefore 1166. His inheritance was split among his daughters: Marger
2 CONC y;Bertha, who married Philip de Brause; and Lucy. Instigated his son in lawHumphrey de Bohun III to rally with Mathilda and defend Trowbridgeagainst King Steven.
2 CONT
2 CONT
