1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Serving twice at the court of Henry II, once as a child hostage and once again later as an emissary, he became fluent in English; hence his nickname, "Sais," meaning "English speaker."  (It can also mean "English" 
2 CONC -- it is the Welsh for "Saxon.")
