2 CONT Gwrwared was followed by his son Gwilym (or William) who led plundering raids on the prebend of Mathry with the result that he was excommunicated by the Church. This occurred between 1175 and 1203 and Sir John Lloyd placed the pro
2 CONC bable date as circa 1195.
2 CONT
