2 CONT The earliest Heilyn who had a son named Iorwerth was Heilyn (1150) ap Cyfnerth (1115) ap Morgeneu (1080) ap Gwrydyr (1045) which continues as above. His son was called Iorwerth Wyddel.
2 CONT
2 CONT The third such Heilyn was Heilyn (1175) ap Cyfnerth (1140) ap Morgeneu Ynad (1110) ap Morgeneu (1080) ap Gwrydyr (1045) as above. Virtually every medieval citation which mentions Morgeneu Ynad assumed he was the same man as Morgen
2 CONC eu ap Gwrydyr (cited very anciently), but one entire branch of the family requires Morganeu Ynad to be born c. 1110 and thus could not be a son of Gwrydyr. While the citations call his son Iorwerth Wyddel, I suggest they added the
2 CONC  "Wyddel" because they assumed this was the same line as the one shown immediately above and did not pay attention to the family timeline.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Steven Ferry, February 25, 2018.)
