1 NAME Tiberius Julius Rhescuporis
2 GIVN Tiberius Julius Rhescuporis
1 NAME Rhescuporis V, king of Bosphorus
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 200
1 DEAT
2 DATE 276
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tiberius Julius Rhescuporis V Philocaesar Philoromaios Eusebes, Prince and Roman Client King of the Bosporan Kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiberius_Julius_Rhescuporis_V
2 CONT
2 CONT Tiberius Julius Rhescuporis V Philocaesar Philoromaios Eusebes, also known as Rhescuporis V (Greek: Τιβέριος Ἰούλιος Ῥησκούπορις Ε' Φιλόκαισαρ Φιλορώμαίος Eυσεbής, Philocaesar Philoromaios Eusebes, means lover of Caesar, lover of 
2 CONC Rome who is the Pius one, flourished 3rd century – died 276) was a prince and Roman Client King of the Bosporan Kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhescuporis V was the son and heir to the Bosporan King Ininthimeus and his mother was an unnamed woman and was of Greek, Iranian and Roman ancestry. Rhescuporis V was named in honor of his paternal uncle, the previous Bosporan Ki
2 CONC ng Rhescuporis IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhescuporis V succeeded when Ininthimeus died in 240. Rhescuporis V reigned as Bosporan King from 240 until his death in 276. His royal title on coins is in Greek: ΒΑΣΙΛΕΩΣ ΡΗΣΚΟΥΠΟΡΙΔΟΣ or of King Rhescuporis. He was a contempora
2 CONC ry to the rule of the Roman Emperors Gordian III, Philip the Arab, Decius and the period Crisis of the Third Century which occurred in the Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to surviving coinage, Rhescuporis V appeared to have been a religious person who was involved in the worship of the Goddess Aphrodite and her cult. Little is known of the reign and life of Rhescuporis V. During his reign
2 CONC , Rhescuporis V co-ruled with his three sons from an unnamed woman and they were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Pharsanzes (253–254) Synges (258–276) Teiranes (275–279)
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhescuporis V died in 276 and was succeeded by his third son, Teiranes.
