1 CONC 297) a fiction that nonetheless conveys political truths (Mackay 1999, 200). That the conversation between the two emperors was purportedly "private" is not necessarily damning: "Conversations between important men...have a way of
1 CONC  becoming public knowledge." (Potter 2004, 338).
