1 CONT   53. ^ Mattingly, 233–34. A number of modern accounts draw parallels the campaigns of Severus and Constantius. The Panegyrici Latini 6(7)7.1ff gives only the usual features of a British campaign—marshes and woods, Caledonians and
1 CONC  Picts—without providing any specifics (Southern 2001, 341). Little of Constantius' movement is visible in the archaeological evidence (Southern 2001, 170). Constantius and Galerius took a Britannici maximi II victory title by Jan
1 CONC uary 7, 306, indicating a campaign in the second half of 305 (L'Année Épigraphique 1961.240; Barnes, Constantine and Eusebius, 298; Elliott, Christianity of Constantine, 39; Odahl, 309).
