0 @N6000000008630646447@ NOTE Also known as Maximian, was Augustus over western half of the Empire, used name Herculius (the servant of Jovius the name chosen by Diocletian), was very reluctantly forced to abdicate 305 when Diocletian abdicated, and allowed hi
1 CONC s Caesar (formed in 292) take over. The Western Caesar was Constantius who had Gaul, Britian and Spain while Maximian had Italy and Africa.
1 CONT Diocletian had Asia and Egypt while his Caesar,(son in law Galerius)had the Balkans.
1 CONT Maximian made Milan focus of empire rather than Rome.. Diocletian made focus of Empire Eastern Empire not Rome/west.
1 CONT In 305 Constantius became Augustus of the West, at Treves (Augusta Trevirorium), Galerius took the Danube and Asia Minor, the two new Ceasars were Daza- better known as Maximan nephew of Galerius,  and  Severus. This was confirmed
1 CONC  by Diocletian as his last public act, ignoring the son of Constantius - Constantine (later "The Great")  and Maxentius son of Maxentius. Daza/Maximan was sent to the East, Severus to the Milan.
1 CONT The empire went to pot. The rich evaded/ avoided not only the old taxes but all new taxes ruining the middle class- the rich got Very Rich and the middle class disappeared into the very poor.
1 CONT In 306 Constantius died at York.
1 CONT Constantine informed Galerius that the Legions had compelled him to assume the title, and Galerius only dared to confirm ratify the appointment/title.
1 CONT Thew senate of Rome wanted to reasert itself and appointed Maxentius as Augustus and a power thirsty Maximan emerged from "retirement" to support this title. Severus marched "hot foot" from Milan, found Rome already lost and event
1 CONC ually was tricked into surrender by Maximan who allowed him to commit "honorable suicide". Maximianus gave his daughter Fausta in marriage to Constantine to cement the status quo and Constantine accepted both offers.
