0 @N6000000002188286974@ NOTE Julia the Elder
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Julia the Elder (October 39 BC - 14), known to her contemporaries as Julia Caesaris filia or Julia Augusti filia (Classical Latin: IVLIA•CAESARIS•FILIA or IVLIA•AVGVSTI•FILIA[1]) was the daughter and only natural child of Augustus
1 CONC . Augustus subsequently adopted several male members of his close family as sons. Julia resulted from Augustus' second marriage with Scribonia, her birth occurring on the same day as Scribonia's divorce from Augustus, who wished t
1 CONC o marry Livia Drusilla.
1 CONT
