1 CONC ssert that Caesar was quaestor in 69. Gelzer then explains that Caesar, after taking on his place of duty, delivered an oration in praise of his aunt Julia. Shortly after this, his wife died too. 
1 CONT ^ This Quintus Servilius Caepio could have been Marcus Junius Brutus (one of Caesar's assassins) who after adopted by his uncle Quintus Servilius Caepio, was known as Quintus Servilius Caepio Brutus for an unknown period of time. 
