0 @N6000000000715084110@ NOTE King of Gwynedd (878-916)
1 CONT
1 CONT Following is from: http://www.britannia.com/history/ebk/ebktime2.html
1 CONT 880  - King Anarawd of Gwynedd initiates a revenge attack on the Mercian armies and defeats them on the River Conwy.
1 CONT c.881  - King Anarawd of Gwynedd and his brothers begin extensive military campaigns to quell resistance in Powys and Seisyllwg.
1 CONT c.885  - Kings Hyfaidd of Dyfed, Elisedd of Brycheiniog and Hywel of Glywysing are harassed by the armies of King Anarawd of Gwynedd. They seek the protection of King Alfred of England and submit to his overlordship. Anarawd seeks
1 CONC  an alliance with the Norse Kings of York.
1 CONT 894  - King Anarawd of Gwynedd's shaky alliance with the Vikings collapses. His kingdom is ravaged by the Norsemen. Anarawd is forced to ask for help from King Alfred of England and submits to his overlordship. Alfred imposes oppr
1 CONC essive terms and forces Anarawd to confirmation in the Christian Church with Alfred as godfather. Bishop Asser of Sherborne, writes his "Life of King Alfred"
1 CONT 895 - King Anarawd of Gwynedd is supplied with English troops to assist in his reconquest of Seisyllwg. He is successful and his brother, King Cadell, is finally able to take his rightful place on the Seisyllwg throne.
1 CONT 916  - Death of King Anarawd of Gwynedd.
