0 @N6000000001744855280@ NOTE [s2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Lucius Weaver, 1928:
1 CONT
1 CONT  CADELL (son of No. 16). In the division of the dominion of his father he was given Deheubarth
1 CONT           and a large part of South Wales. His brother Merfyn received Powys. He and his brothers made so
1 CONT           much trouble for the neighboring kingdoms that they were compelled to seek help from Alfred the
1 CONT           Great. In 893 he was attacked by his brother Anarawd, King of Gwynedd, who invaded and
1 CONT           plundered Seisyllwg. After the death of his brother Merfyn, Cadell drove out his nephews and
1 CONT           appropriated Powys to himself. He died about 909 and his kingdom was divided between his sons,
1 CONT           Hywel and Clydog.
1 CONT
1 CONT           In the Mostyn Manuscript No. 117 the pedigree of his distinguished descendant, Llewelyn ap Gruffyd,
1 CONT           is traced back through Cadell to "Adam, Son of God." If the compiler did not draw on his imagination
1 CONT           for parts of this pedigree he must have had access to records not now in existence.Lucius Weaver, 1928:
1 CONT
1 CONT  CADELL (son of No. 16). In the division of the dominion of his father he was given Deheubarth
1 CONT           and a large part of South Wales. His brother Merfyn received Powys. He and his brothers made so
1 CONT           much trouble for the neighboring kingdoms that they were compelled to seek help from Alfred the
1 CONT           Great. In 893 he was attacked by his brother Anarawd, King of Gwynedd, who invaded and
1 CONT           plundered Seisyllwg. After the death of his brother Merfyn, Cadell drove out his nephews and
1 CONT           appropriated Powys to himself. He died about 909 and his kingdom was divided between his sons,
1 CONT           Hywel and Clydog.
1 CONT
1 CONT           In the Mostyn Manuscript No. 117 the pedigree of his distinguished descendant, Llewelyn ap Gruffyd,
1 CONT           is traced back through Cadell to "Adam, Son of God." If the compiler did not draw on his imagination
1 CONT           for parts of this pedigree he must have had access to records not now in existence.
0 @N6000000002248215041@ NOTE Cadell ap Rhodri Mawr, King of Seisyllwg in South Wales, followed the lead of his brother Anarawd ap Rhodri Mawr, King of Gwynedd, abandoned an alliance with the Danish Kingdom of York and acknowledged Ælfred the Great as overlord
1 CONC . The precise nature of this overlordship is not known, and there was an attempt to portray this submission as a desire for unity among Christian rulers against the pagan Danes. However, this recognition by Welsh rulers that that 
1 CONC the King of England had claims upon them would be a central fact in the subsequent history of Wales. 
1 CONT Died in 909. 
1 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri Mawr had the following children: 
1 CONT Hywel Dda (the Good) ap Cadell, Prince of Deheubarth
0 @N6000000002187763399@ NOTE Cadell ap Rhodri
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri (854–909) was the son of Rhodri Mawr ("the Great"). He inherited the kingdom of Seisyllwg from his father in 878, and passed it to his son, Hywel Dda ("the Good"), on his death in 909. Cadell and Hywel had previou
1 CONC sly conquered Dyfed in 904/905, establishing Hywel as the king in that region. After his father's death, Hywel merged the two kingdoms to establish Deheubarth.
1 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri
1 CONT Dinefwr Dynasty
1 CONT Born: 854 Died: 909
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Rhodri the Great Prince of Seisyllwg
1 CONT 854-909 Merged by Hywel Dda into Deheubarth
