1 CONC  Foel.
1 CONT In 952 Iago and Ieuaf invaded the south, penetrating as far as Dyfed. The sons of Hywel retaliated by invading the north in 954, reaching as far north as the Conwy valley before being defeated in a battle at Llanrwst and being obl
1 CONC iged to retreat to Ceredigion.   Rhodri died in 953 and Edwin in 954, leaving Owain to rule Deheubarth alone. Owain did not again try to reclaim Gwynedd, but instead he and his son Einon turned eastwards to attack the kingdom of M
1 CONC organnwg (modern Glamorgan) in 960, 970 and 977. Owain was now ageing, and it appears that Einon took over the rule of the kingdom on behalf of his father. On a further raid on the east in 984, Einon was killed by the noblemen of 
1 CONC Gwent.
1 CONT Following Einon's death, Owain's second son, Maredudd, took over the leadership in war, and in 986 did what his father had failed to do by seizing the throne of Gwynedd, ousting Ieuaf's son Cadwallon ab Ieuaf. The following year O
1 CONC wain died and Maredudd became king of Deheubarth as well as Gwynedd.
0 @N6000000004533093284@ NOTE Owain and his two brothers, Rhodri, d. 953, & Edwin, d. 954, werejointly kings of Deheubarth (Seisyllwg and Dyfed).  The youngest,Owain, was sole king from 954.
0 @N6000000001744855201@ NOTE [s2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT OWAIN (son of No. 18). On the death of his father Gwynedd and Powys rebelled and were lost
1 CONT           to the house of Hywel Dha in the battle of Nant Carno. His brothers having died Owain was now sole
1 CONT           ruler of Deheubarth. As a military leader he does not appear to have made a brilliant record. The
1 CONT           Danes made him much trouble. In 959 he demolished two colleges because they received Saxon
1 CONT           students. He was proud of his ancestry and he compiled a record on his father's side extending back
1 CONT           to Cunedda and on his mother's side to Vorteporix, King of Dyfed, who flourished between A.D. 500
1 CONT           and 600. These pedigrees may be found in Harleian MS. 3859. In the Annales Cambriae his pedigree
1 CONT           is the first one given and it extends back to the beginning of the Christian era. The early generations
1 CONT           may be legendary, but a very conservative authority, Sir John Rhys, writes of it as follows: "It is a
1 CONT           genuinely old compilation, and however much we may doubt or rather be in a state of indifference as
1 CONT           to the more remote stages, yet if we bear in mind the legal structure and general complexion of the
1 CONT           community in which it was produced it would be an excessive display of the skeptical spirit to deny its
1 CONT           accuracy for many generations." In 986, being old and feeble, he abdicated in favor of his son
1 CONT           Maredudd. He died in 987 or 988.OWAIN (son of No. 18). On the death of his father Gwynedd and Powys rebelled and were lost
1 CONT           to the house of Hywel Dha in the battle of Nant Carno. His brothers having died Owain was now sole
1 CONT           ruler of Deheubarth. As a military leader he does not appear to have made a brilliant record. The
1 CONT           Danes made him much trouble. In 959 he demolished two colleges because they received Saxon
1 CONT           students. He was proud of his ancestry and he compiled a record on his father's side extending back
1 CONT           to Cunedda and on his mother's side to Vorteporix, King of Dyfed, who flourished between A.D. 500
1 CONT           and 600. These pedigrees may be found in Harleian MS. 3859. In the Annales Cambriae his pedigree
1 CONT           is the first one given and it extends back to the beginning of the Christian era. The early generations
1 CONT           may be legendary, but a very conservative authority, Sir John Rhys, writes of it as follows: "It is a
1 CONT           genuinely old compilation, and however much we may doubt or rather be in a state of indifference as
1 CONT           to the more remote stages, yet if we bear in mind the legal structure and general complexion of the
1 CONT           community in which it was produced it would be an excessive display of the skeptical spirit to deny its
1 CONT           accuracy for many generations." In 986, being old and feeble, he abdicated in favor of his son
1 CONT           Maredudd. He died in 987 or 988.
