0 @N6000000002187905273@ NOTE Maredudd ab Owain
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Maredudd ap Owain (died 999) was a Prince of Gwynedd and of Deheubarth.
1 CONT
1 CONT Maredydd was the grandson of Hywel Dda. His father, Owain ap Hywel Dda, was king of Deheubarth. As Owain grew too old to lead in battle his son Maredydd took his place, and in 986 captured Gwynedd from Cadwallon ab Ieuaf. On Owain
1 CONC 's death in 988 Maredydd also became ruler of Deheubarth. He may have controlled all Wales apart from Gwent and Morgannwg.
1 CONT
1 CONT He is recorded as raiding Mercian settlements on the borders of Radnor and as paying a ransom of one penny a head to rescue some of his subjects who had been taken captive in Viking raids. Danish raids were a constant problem duri
1 CONC ng Maredudd's reign. In 987 Godfrey Haroldson raided Anglesey, killing one thousand and carrying away two thousand as captives. Maredudd died in 999 and was described by the annalists as "the most famous king of the Britons". Foll
1 CONC owing his death, the throne of Gwynedd was recovered for the line of Idwal Foel by Cynan ap Hywel.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT References
1 CONT John Edward Lloyd (1911). A history of Wales: from the earliest times to the Edwardian conquest. Longmans, Green & Co. 
1 CONT Dinefwr Dynasty
1 CONT Born: Unknown; Died: 999 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Cadwallon ab Ieuaf King of Gwynedd
1 CONT 986-999 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Cynan ap Hywel 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Owain ap Hywel King of Deheubarth
1 CONT 988-999 
0 @N6000000001744843038@ NOTE [s2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT MAREDUDD (son of No. 19). He became King of Deheubarth in 986 and directly proceeded to
1 CONT           conquer Gwynedd. In 990 he raided and plundered Maes Hyfaidd (Radnorshire) which was then in
1 CONT           the possession of the Mercians. In the same year the Saxons devastated his territory and in 993 it was
1 CONT           wasted by the plague. Both the Danes and the Saxons caused him much trouble during his entire reign.
1 CONT           His nephews also tried to regain Gwynedd, but he was successful over all his enemies. It is said that
1 CONT           he obtained Powys through his mother which made him King of all Wales. In the Bruts he is acclaimed
1 CONT           as the "most famous King of the Britons." (Lloyd). He died in 998 or 999 leaving an only daughter and
1 CONT           sole heiress, Angharad. She married Llewelyn ap Seisyll, who assumed the reins of government. They
1 CONT           had one son, Gruffydd.
1 CONT Llewelyn died in 1023 and the kingdom was held by others until 1039 when the son, Gruffydd,
1 CONT           succeeded to the throne. Angharad took unto herself a second husband, Cynfyn, and their record is
1 CONT           given in No. 21.MAREDUDD (son of No. 19). He became King of Deheubarth in 986 and directly proceeded to
1 CONT           conquer Gwynedd. In 990 he raided and plundered Maes Hyfaidd (Radnorshire) which was then in
1 CONT           the possession of the Mercians. In the same year the Saxons devastated his territory and in 993 it was
1 CONT           wasted by the plague. Both the Danes and the Saxons caused him much trouble during his entire reign.
1 CONT           His nephews also tried to regain Gwynedd, but he was successful over all his enemies. It is said that
1 CONT           he obtained Powys through his mother which made him King of all Wales. In the Bruts he is acclaimed
1 CONT           as the "most famous King of the Britons." (Lloyd). He died in 998 or 999 leaving an only daughter and
1 CONT           sole heiress, Angharad. She married Llewelyn ap Seisyll, who assumed the reins of government. They
1 CONT           had one son, Gruffydd.
1 CONT Llewelyn died in 1023 and the kingdom was held by others until 1039 when the son, Gruffydd,
1 CONT           succeeded to the throne. Angharad took unto herself a second husband, Cynfyn, and their record is
1 CONT           given in No. 21.
0 @N6000000002248212982@ NOTE Maredudd ap Owain, Prince of Deheubarth who succeeded his father Owain ap Hywel Dha as ruler of South Wales/Deheubarth in 986. Maredudd conquered Gwynedd and temporarily united Wales once more, but his reign was a troubled one. Fr
1 CONC om their strongholds in Dublin and the Isle of Man, the Norsemen ravaged the coast of Wales. It was recorded in 987 that two thousand men of the island of Anglesey were seized and sold as slaves. In 989 Maredudd was obliged to rai
1 CONC se a penny poll-tax to bribe the Norsemen to stay away. 
1 CONT Died in 999. 
1 CONT Maredudd ap Owain had the following children: 
1 CONT Cadwallon ap Maredudd 
1 CONT Angharad Ferch Maredudd, Queen of Powys
