0 @N6000000001353929331@ NOTE Madoc ap Meredith, Prince of Lower Powys, from him called Powys Fadoc, who d. at Winchester in 1160, and was buried in Meifod Church, nearMathrafal, his castle-palace on the banks of the Vwrnwy, where the carved stone lid of his c
1 CONC offin, with the cognizance of the dragon, is still to be seen. According to the Welsh chronicle, he was "one who feared God and relieved the poor."
