1 CONT Hadrianus IV, Pope 
1 CONT Henry Plantagenet 
1 CONT Stephen I died in 1154 and Henry Plantagenet became Henry II of England. He was descended from William the Conqueror and through his mother, Matilda, from the Anglo-Saxons.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Eleanor of Aquitaine who had been married to Louis VII of France and so Aquitaine passed from France to England.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry II saw the need for central government. He wanted to strengthen his control of Scotland, Wales and Ireland. In 1157 Malcolm of Scotland paid homage to Henry and Scotland did not regain her independence until Richard I's reig
1 CONC n.
1 CONT
1 CONT Wales continued to be fractious and it was not until 1176 that the Welsh made their peace with Henry. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Ireland was next. 
1 CONT
1 CONT HENRY II (1133-1189)
1 CONT
1 CONT Aged 14 he was fighting for his mother's claim to the English throne
1 CONT In 1151 his father died and he became Count of Anjou and Duke of Normandy
1 CONT In 1152 he married Eleanor of Aquitaine
1 CONT In 1154 he became King of England
1 CONT In 1171 he invaded Ireland and was recognised as Lord by nearly all the Irish kings
1 CONT In 1173 the Count of Toulouse paid homage
1 CONT In 1173 his wife and sons turned against him and he quarrelled fatally with his one time friend Thomas Becket Archbishop of Canterbury
1 CONT Created the judicial system and the Common Law
1 CONT Died 1189, Richard I became King
